        "id": 158921,
        "name": "Rabk",
        "username": "Rabk",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/rabk/{size}/1978_2.png",
        "created_at": "2016-02-05T21:33:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"jffdougan\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/jffdougan/48/1882_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> jffdougan:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>the only one that threw me for a loop was seeing Ra: Hoth. given some of the other abbreviations, I could totally see \"Beard Ra\" as being a workable shorthand.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Horus Ra maybe? Was trying to stay somewhat close to the official names while still fitting in the space requirements.</p>\n<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"jffdougan\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/jffdougan/48/1882_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> jffdougan:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Ninjedit: And maybe do something to distinguish the two version of Plague Rat, La Cap, Ambuscade, and Miss Info?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>There's only one version of each of those though. The only character with two tokens is The Operative/Zhu Long's Operative. <br><br></p>\n<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"jffdougan\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/jffdougan/48/1882_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> jffdougan:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p><b>mwc146 wrote:</b></p>\n<div><blockquote>Huh, usually I see Absolute Zero abbreviated \"AZ\", but A0 makes sense, too.</blockquote></div>\nYeah, I do AZ myself, but I was able to figure that one out. \n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Easy enough to change it to AZ instead of A0. Since my originals were handwritten and I write my zeroes with a slash it never occured to me to do it differently. (My group calls him \"A-naught\" when speaking.)</p>",
